\subsection{18-Parameter Real-Data Estimation}
\label{subsec:results_18param_kalman}

I estimate the 18-parameter SW07 specification using a Kalman filter with MH sampling on US data (1959Q1--2004Q4, 184 quarters, 7 observables). Table~\ref{tab:18param_posterior} reports the posterior. Key findings: $\sigma_b$ revises from 1.85 to 0.12 (tenfold reduction), $\xi_w$ is near its upper bound at 0.95, and $\varepsilon_p$ rises from 10 to 39---indicating substantial real rigidities. Log-likelihood at posterior mean: $-1{,}040$.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Posterior Summary: 18-Parameter Kalman Filter Estimation}
\label{tab:18param_posterior}
\begin{tabular}{llrrrr}
\toprule
Parameter & Description & Init & Post.\ Mean & Q5 & Q95 \\
\midrule
\multicolumn{6}{l}{\textit{Shock Persistence}} \\
$\rho_a$ & TFP & 0.990 & 0.987 & 0.982 & 0.990 \\
